{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792263125,"nonce":"laqAxaWWoKX+qZkPYbs2j25mMGo=","title":"A full tree rebuild has no owner scope, so what its widgets create is never disposed","message":"`Owner` (blinc_core/src/owner.rs) disposes the signals, computeds and effects made inside `Owner::run`, but only a region row runs its build under one (region.rs). The runners rebuild the whole tree on a window resize and other full rebuilds (`ws.needs_rebuild = true`, windowed.rs), and that build runs under no owner. Everything a widget creates while building is therefore kept for the life of the process: each bound widget's computeds, and every effect.\n\nEffects are the costly part, since they run eagerly on each write to what they read. Examples made during a widget build: cn number_input's `show_state_in_field` and the OTP's `show_value_in_slots` (an effect per build, writing into the previous build's field data), plus the computeds every text_input, text_area, cn button/checkbox/etc. makes. A window resized 20 times leaves 20 dead effects per number input, all running on every change to its value. Keyed state (`use_state_keyed`) is meant to outlive a rebuild and is separate (483c864).\n\nFix: have each runner hold an `Owner` per window, run every full build inside it, and dispose it when the next full build replaces the tree (windowed, web, iOS and Android each have the build step). Widgets already built to create their effects inside the build need nothing more. Check afterwards that keyed state and anything a widget deliberately keeps across a rebuild is made outside the scope (`bind_bool_targets` and friends dedupe by signal and are created once).","files":null}]}